e associated with recent pandemic strains of Vibrio parahaemolyticus</article-title><source>Emerg Infect Dis</source><year>2001</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>477</fpage><lpage>478</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11384535</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nasu</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Iida</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Sugahara</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamaichi</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>KS</given-names></name><name><surname>Yokoyama</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Makino</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Shinagawa</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Honda</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A filamentous phage associated with recent pandemic Vibrio parahaemolyticus O3:K6 strains</article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source><year>2000</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>2156</fpage><lpage>2161</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10834969</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>TL</given-names></name><name><surname>Musser</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Nordstrom</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>DePaola</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Monday</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Identification of a protein biomarker unique to the pandemic O3:K6 clone of Vibrio parahaemolyticus</article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source><year>2004</year><volume>42</volume><fpage>1657</fpage><lpage>1665</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15071022</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/JCM